{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1242242-more-details-on-the-mask-and-other-lore-clarifications","id":1242242,"title":"More Details On The Mask (And Other Lore Clarifications)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-02T22:42:31-07:00","id":1242242,"title":"More Details On The Mask (And Other Lore Clarifications)","content":"I'm unclear on a few key pieces of lore in the book and I was wondering if one of the developers could clarify them. <hr /><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Mask</span></b><br /> <br /> The book says unfortunately little about the Mask in comparison to the Mien. Do you look like your former self? In the past you haven't necessarily, yet one of the short stories in the book has a character recognize a Changeling by name after their escape with a simple look. This left it pretty ambiguous for me. Suppose your Mask doesn't look like your former self then. Is there any rhyme or reason to its appearance? It doesn't look like you, but is it similar? If not, are there any limitations to the random nature of the Mask? Does it have to share your age, your race, your sex?<br /> <br /> Does the book intend to be this vague? It feels like an oversight. Even the appearance of items with a Mask are given a more detailed description. This is odd since this is a game in which the first thing a player might do is investigate their old lives, and as ST I currently have no idea how that would actually play out.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">True (Fae) Lies</span></b><br /> <br /> The book contradicts itself several times over the 'truthiness' of True Fae. I'd like to drop a few examples. I hope that's okay.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The True Fae are liars. You know that now. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The True Fae are bound by their word \u2014 even their lies are partial truths and unspoken information, rather than outright falsehoods. A Keeper might fail to point out a loophole in a contract, or abide only by the razor-sharp fine points of a deal, but to outright break a sworn promise is anathema to them. Many cannot even understand humanity\u2019s ability to do so with ease. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Promises are worth less than nothing without a contract to back them up. You know, because you heard so many and every one of them was a lie. \u201cOf course you can go home, if you build one toy for each good little moppet on Earth. \u2018Tis child\u2019s play, for one with your skill!\u201d \u201cI\u2019ll set you free as soon as the war is over, my dear, but I so desperately need you to bring all my dead soldiers back to life each morning.\u201d \u201cBe my lady-in-waiting for a hundred and one years, just that! and soon you\u2019ll be on your way.\u201d You worked your fingers to the bone, hunched over your workbench or running yourself ragged in the fields, day in and day out. All that, for a glimmer of hope \u2014 surely this time your Keeper would cleave to his word. He never did. </div> </div> </div>Could someone clarify this since it seems so important? You could argue that some of the promises on that list were half truths, but the words 'lie' and 'liar' are fairly clear so I don't think I'm reading too much into this. It's my suspicion that Fae actually do understand lying perfectly well and use it whenever they can get away with it, but lying carries huge <i>risks </i>for Fae like losing Titles and Regalia tokens. As such they wouldn't lie to someone that <i>knows</i> this. I might be way off though. <hr /><br /> Thank you in advance for any answers or other discussion!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24472,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24472-corablue","user":"CoraBlue","date":". 08-03-2018, 01:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24472-corablue","name":"CoraBlue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-02T23:26:27-07:00","id":1242250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoraBlue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1242242-more-details-on-the-mask-and-other-lore-clarifications#post1242242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If not, are there any limitations to the random nature of the Mask? Does it have to share your age, your race, your sex?</div> </div> </div> </div>The literature that informs Changeling's headspace allows for the Mask of a changeling to be a distortion of their mortal self to account for those drastic alterations to their form that have stuck, but a common narrative angle the fae-touched approach their promise-bound from is that they'd recognize them anywhere.<br /> <br /> There has never been a particularly strong implication that, absent specific effects to the contrary, your Mask is any less than noticeably referent to what you looked like as a mortal after accounting for any changes brought about by age or supernaturally-induced lifestyle shifts \u2014 you might be missing your nose and heavily tanned after a lifetime under the beating hot sun of a salamander's gladiator arena, but if you were a Chinese woman then that process has rather low odds of resulting in you coming out of your durance with the features of a Moroccan man without direct intervention by your Keeper to that effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Could someone clarify this since it seems so important? You could argue that some of the promises on that list were half truths, but the words 'lie' and 'liar' are fairly clear so I don't think I'm reading too much into this. </div> </div> </div>The True Fae do not break a sworn promise without duress. This does not mean that every assurance they offer is a sworn promise \u2014 recall that their words cannot be sealed by lesser fae and a contract is only enforced if it's enforceable.<br /> <br /> Their reputation for misleading people with incomplete information is not meaningfully different from a reputation as a tricky liar in how it necessitates reminders of their enormous capacity for and will to dishonest dealing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T17:17:33-07:00","id":1242536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your Mask is ... noticeably referent to what you looked like as a mortal after accounting for any changes brought about by age or supernaturally-induced lifestyle shifts </div> </div> </div>In other words, your Mask is based on your Mien, which is based on you. That guideline, even if accurate, isn't particularly helpful. Changelings who become fire or music don't really have a human appearance to base anything off of. In addition there are stories in the book of denizens of Arcadia who emerge into the world as Changelings despite no human past at all (The Boulder). Saying something like, &quot;They look as tough as a rock,&quot; only gets you so far.<br /> <br /> Then we have examples of Faetouched who are also perhaps Changelings despite having no Keeper at all, such as the woman who lost her face in the Hedge and made a new one after several years.<br /> <br /> I appreciate the attempt to pull from inspirational material but that's not helpful here. Mirrormask, Labyrinth, Over the Gardenwall, etc. These are all books and films which feature either no Mask or a Mask that is identical to their Doppelgangers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The True Fae do not break a sworn promise without duress. This does not mean that every assurance they offer is a sworn promise \u2014 recall that their words cannot be sealed by lesser fae and a contract is only enforced if it's enforceable. </div> </div> </div>I feel like this is a non-answer. Which isn't your fault, I just firmly believe the book doesn't provide enough information. Yes, there is technically a difference between a promise and a sworn promise, but to a Changeling, especially one recently taken, there is no distinction. The Fae lie and break promises, this much is given as fact in 2e. And since all other fae are lesser fae to the Gentry I feel like perhaps these semantics aren't helpful. There aren't many likely scenarios where other Gentry will put up with the incredible inconvenience of not only presiding over a contract but enforcing it as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24472,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24472-corablue","user":"CoraBlue","date":". 08-03-2018, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24472-corablue","name":"CoraBlue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T17:54:50-07:00","id":1242551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoraBlue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1242242-more-details-on-the-mask-and-other-lore-clarifications?p=1242536#post1242536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other words, your Mask is based on your Mien, which is based on you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. Your Mask is based on <i>what you used to look like</i>, potentially subject to changes that people can normally undergo in regular life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In addition there are stories in the book of denizens of Arcadia who emerge into the world as Changelings despite no human past at all (The Boulder). Saying something like, &quot;They look as tough as a rock,&quot; only gets you so far. </div> </div> </div>This has basically nothing to do with the question of what your Mask looks like in relation to your past appearance, because the problem you face here is identical to any other NPC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Changelings who become fire or music </div> </div> </div>\u2026Don't have Masks, because those kids are still in Arcadia. Keep the goalposts where they were.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I appreciate the attempt to pull from inspirational material but that's not helpful here. Mirrormask, Labyrinth, Over the Gardenwall, etc. These are all books and films which feature either no Mask or a Mask that is identical to their Doppelgangers. </div> </div> </div>The inspirational material I'm pulling from here is stuff like the explicitly mentioned &quot;parents that can always recognize their child.&quot;<br /> <br /> Unless you were specifically kidnapped by a creature that made a habit of mutilating your face and forcing you to learn an entirely different way to move through your everyday, your Mask is going to look like you in the absence of magic to the contrary. Your fetch may look like a you that went down a completely road in life, but the game is not generally written to assume that multiple core identifiers of your physical body have changed completely from your time in Arcadia as a matter of course. You might look older and tanner and leaner meaner, but you haven't stopped being an Indian kid from the south of London just because you went to Faerie.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like this is a non-answer. Which isn't your fault, I just firmly believe the book doesn't provide enough information. Yes, there is technically a difference between a promise and a sworn promise, but to a Changeling, especially one recently taken, there is no distinction. The Fae lie and break promises, this much is given as fact in 2e. And since all other fae are lesser fae to the Gentry I feel like perhaps these semantics aren't helpful. There aren't many likely scenarios where other Gentry will put up with the incredible inconvenience of not only presiding over a contract but enforcing it as well. </div> </div> </div><i>That is the point.</i> The Fae make pledges and keep them as a matter of basic common sense. If you can maneuver them into saying something unwise and meaning it, you have leverage on them, but the rest of the time it is wisest to assume they are all too prepared to take you for a ride.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 08-03-2018, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T18:11:31-07:00","id":1242555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Changelings who become fire or music\u2026Don't have Masks, because those kids are still in Arcadia. Keep the goalposts where they were. </div> </div> </div>I think you might be misunderstanding me. I don't mean to be confrontational. They would have Masks once they leave though? And my question is what system do we use to determine what a Mask looks like based on some concrete rules? And if they are based on what you used to look like wouldn't that mean you more or less look the same? Does that have to be the case? These are unanswered questions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This has basically nothing to do with the question of what your Mask looks like in relation to your past appearance </div> </div> </div>Who's moving goalposts now? Politely, my question has always been what system do we use to determine what a Mask looks like and if there are hard limits. That is especially relevant to a Changeling who has no human past.<br /> <br /> I think I'd rather hear from the actual devs. No offense meant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24472-corablue","name":"CoraBlue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24472_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T18:27:51-07:00","id":1242558,"title":"","content":"If we don\u2019t need concrete guidelines for designing what mortal characters look like now and how they look like after years, then we don\u2019t need guidelines for changelings\u2019 Masks. <br /> <br /> Also, changelings without human pasts? Did I miss something, or did the game significantly change? Changeling always was about people taken to Faerie and changed by the experience, wasn\u2019t it? Or at least, that was the assumption for <i>player character</i> changelings, much like how in Vampire it\u2019s assumed you\u2019re a human turned vampire, not an embodied Strix or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T18:39:50-07:00","id":1242566,"title":"","content":"No such thing as a changeling without a human past. Hobgoblins and Strangers who project a mask in the mortal world look like a mortal version of their fae selves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-03-2018, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T20:22:03-07:00","id":1242588,"title":"","content":"The Mask looks like they did before they were taken, adjusted to fit their new form. A changeling who functioned as a formless bonfire in Arcadia may have blazed out of there in a massive forest fire, but as soon as they hit the Hedge, they\u2019ll take on a humanoid form that strongly resembles a fiery version of their original form. Maybe they\u2019re a little flushed and tend to be twitchy, but they still look like themselves. A Gargantuan that constantly banged his head on the stars in Arcadia shrinks down to an impressively large but still humanly possible size, looking like himself only larger. \u201cDave, did you go through a growth spurt?\u201d For those that got smaller? Well, they might seem like they\u2019ve withered or become malnourished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T13:16:12-07:00","id":1243004,"title":"","content":"So, if I may be so bold as to summarize (Summer-ize?): <br /> <br /> 1. The Mein is what your impossible fae-form of stories and imagination got hammered into when you left the freedom of your prison in Arcadia. It will assume a generally human form based on core identifiers that tend not to get messed with by the Fae thanks to reasons--though they certainly could if they cared to enough.<br /> <br /> 2. The Mask continues the trend of making you fit in, taking cues from your perception of yourself and the form that the Mein assumed under the unrelenting pressure of Ironside. Unless you have become an unrecognizable person <b><i>inside, </i></b>then you will have recognizable characteristics (mannerisms, appearance quirks at minimum) that someone who knows you (especially who knows you well) will pick up on and find familiar.<br /> <br /> Is that... sufficient?<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T16:10:21-07:00","id":1243053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1242242-more-details-on-the-mask-and-other-lore-clarifications?p=1243004#post1243004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. The Mein is what your impossible fae-form of stories and imagination got hammered into when you left the freedom of your prison in Arcadia. It will assume a generally human form based on core identifiers that tend not to get messed with by the Fae thanks to reasons--though they certainly could if they cared to enough.<br /> <br /> 2. The Mask continues the trend of making you fit in, taking cues from your perception of yourself and the form that the Mein assumed under the unrelenting pressure of Ironside. Unless you have become an unrecognizable person <b><i>inside, </i></b>then you will have recognizable characteristics (mannerisms, appearance quirks at minimum) that someone who knows you (especially who knows you well) will pick up on and find familiar.<br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. And your mien is humanoid because even if your form in Arcadia was something truly bizarre, that bizarre form can't sustain itself in the mundane world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CoraBlue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1242242-more-details-on-the-mask-and-other-lore-clarifications?p=1242555#post1242555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you might be misunderstanding me. I don't mean to be confrontational. They would have Masks once they leave though? And my question is what system do we use to determine what a Mask looks like based on some concrete rules? And if they are based on what you used to look like wouldn't that mean you more or less look the same? Does that have to be the case? These are unanswered questions.<br /> <br /> Who's moving goalposts now? Politely, my question has always been what system do we use to determine what a Mask looks like and if there are hard limits. That is especially relevant to a Changeling who has no human past.<br /> <br /> I think I'd rather hear from the actual devs. No offense meant.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are no concrete rules, by design. Your questions are answered through examples and description in chapters 2 and 3. If you want your character's Mask to have changed, cool--do that. If you don't, cool--do that.<br /> <br /> And yeah, there aren't changelings who weren't once human, barring something really weird happening. Which is possible, but an edge case that would be something you and your Storyteller would work out between you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Meghan Fitzgerald | Onyx Path freelance writer &amp; developer</i><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><i>Changeling: The Lost developer</i></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#009999\"><i>Mage: The Awakening developer</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2229-meghan-fitzgerald","name":"Meghan Fitzgerald","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"124"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T10:09:05-07:00","id":1243834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meghan Fitzgerald</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1242242-more-details-on-the-mask-and-other-lore-clarifications?p=1243053#post1243053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. And your mien is humanoid because even if your form in Arcadia was something truly bizarre, that bizarre form can't sustain itself in the mundane world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... I suppose you *might* get a talking Changeling dog by taking a human, changing them into a dog, and changing their fundamental perception of themselves to match.<br /> <br /> Maybe? But again, if you're that far gone you'd probably never leave. <br /> <br /> If there's enough &quot;you&quot; left for reality to get purchase on, it'll try to &quot;fix&quot; you, amiright?<br /> <br /> After all, on Ironside no one knows you're a dog.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}